1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:06,260
Over the past 50 years, JEI has built
deep expertise in learning design.

2
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:11,230
Now, by combining that expertise with
AI, we aim to deliver learning optimized

3
00:00:11,285 --> 00:00:15,500
for every student and set a new global
standard for AI-powered math learning.

4
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:19,335
Here is our plan: building
an AI personalized learning

5
00:00:19,395 --> 00:00:22,090
platform based on the
JEI Math Knowledge Map.

6
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:28,120
The foundation of this platform
is the JEI Math Knowledge Map.

7
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:33,194
For AI to give each student exactly what
they need, it must understand how learning

8
00:00:33,248 --> 00:00:37,290
objectives relate to one another, and
in what order they should be learned.

9
00:00:39,390 --> 00:00:43,030
Think of it as connecting countless
stars scattered across space.

10
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:46,075
We define how individual
learning objectives

11
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:48,620
connect and organize
them into one network.

12
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:51,750
Each point represents
a learning objective.

13
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:55,184
The lines between points
show how skills build on one

14
00:00:55,239 --> 00:00:58,450
another, such as prerequisite
and follow-up relationships.

15
00:00:58,950 --> 00:01:03,040
Line color and thickness show the
type and strength of each connection.

16
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:09,244
With this network, AI can understand
the overall structure of math learning,

17
00:01:09,298 --> 00:01:12,970
and decide what each student needs
to review and what to learn next.

18
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:18,297
We’re building the JEI Math
Knowledge Map around JEI’s

19
00:01:18,357 --> 00:01:21,823
educational philosophy, along
with our workbooks, learning

20
00:01:21,883 --> 00:01:25,170
objectives, and curricula
from Korea and North America.

21
00:01:25,770 --> 00:01:29,257
AI then compares these with
textbooks, curricula, and learning

22
00:01:29,314 --> 00:01:32,745
standards from different countries,
including the U.S. Common

23
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:36,570
Core State Standards, and proposes
how learning objectives connect.

24
00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:41,240
JEI researchers review these
proposals for educational soundness.

25
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:45,630
The result is a global math knowledge
map, one that isn’t tied to any

26
00:01:45,685 --> 00:01:49,860
single country’s curriculum and can be
used anywhere, in Korea and overseas.

27
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:53,030
We call it the JEI Math Universe.

28
00:01:55,130 --> 00:01:59,039
By aligning this global map with each
country’s curriculum, we can develop

29
00:01:59,092 --> 00:02:02,790
and validate learning content for
different markets much more quickly.

30
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:06,760
When we enter a new market, we
don’t have to start from scratch.

31
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:10,142
We connect that country’s
curriculum and learning standards

32
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:12,730
to the knowledge map, and
build the content we need.

33
00:02:14,830 --> 00:02:18,488
And by linking each student’s results
to the map, we can see what they

34
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:22,460
understand, where they need help, and
how their learning changes over time.

35
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:26,642
In short, the JEI Math Knowledge
Map helps us develop products

36
00:02:26,699 --> 00:02:30,570
for each market faster, and personalize
learning for every student.

37
00:02:32,670 --> 00:02:37,330
The platform has three connected layers:
knowledge, AI engine, and service.

38
00:02:37,830 --> 00:02:40,350
We build them step by
step, from the bottom up.

39
00:02:40,950 --> 00:02:44,835
The knowledge layer turns JEI’s
learning materials and educational

40
00:02:44,894 --> 00:02:48,720
expertise into the knowledge map,
a shared foundation AI can use.

41
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:53,282
The AI engine layer
uses that foundation to

42
00:02:53,339 --> 00:02:56,030
generate content and
analyze learning progress.

43
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:01,228
Finally, the service layer
delivers these capabilities

44
00:03:01,286 --> 00:03:03,810
to students through POD
and online learning.

45
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:09,847
Once built, the knowledge layer stays
relatively stable, while the service

46
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:13,730
layer can evolve quickly as technology
and learning environments change.

47
00:03:15,830 --> 00:03:19,430
Seven interconnected projects
will move forward in two phases.

48
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:25,620
Phase 1 focuses on the knowledge map
and automated content generation.

49
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:29,213
AI creates programmed learning
materials in advance,

50
00:03:29,270 --> 00:03:31,860
and we deliver them
through personalized POD.

51
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:37,532
Phase 2 expands into online
learning through progress analysis,

52
00:03:37,588 --> 00:03:40,650
adaptive learning paths, and
an AI learning assistant.

53
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:44,575
The system analyzes each student’s
understanding and progress

54
00:03:44,630 --> 00:03:47,900
as they learn, and adjusts their
learning path in real time.

55
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,921
Throughout both phases, LLM Wiki
serves as a shared knowledge base

56
00:03:53,981 --> 00:03:58,140
that organizes JEI’s educational
knowledge and supports every project.

57
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,630
The centerpiece of Phase
1 is personalized POD.

58
00:04:04,330 --> 00:04:08,165
First, we analyze each student’s
assessment results and learning history

59
00:04:08,218 --> 00:04:11,840
to identify what they need to study
and how much practice they need.

60
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:17,050
AI generates programmed learning materials
in advance for each learning objective.

61
00:04:17,550 --> 00:04:21,870
JEI researchers review them, and
they’re stored in a content database.

62
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:24,818
From this reviewed content, we create and

63
00:04:24,875 --> 00:04:27,510
print personalized
materials for each student.

64
00:04:29,610 --> 00:04:32,692
The student’s results then shape
the next round of learning,

65
00:04:32,743 --> 00:04:36,030
adding review where needed and
adjusting the amount of practice.

66
00:04:36,630 --> 00:04:39,474
We’ll launch this service
in the United States first,

67
00:04:39,528 --> 00:04:42,050
validate the results, and
then expand to Korea.

68
00:04:44,150 --> 00:04:46,800
In Phase 2, we extend
this approach online.

69
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:52,052
Along with correct and incorrect answers,
the system analyzes learning behaviors,

70
00:04:52,108 --> 00:04:55,930
including time spent on problems,
hint usage, and repeated attempts.

71
00:04:56,430 --> 00:04:59,001
It uses those insights
to adjust each student’s

72
00:04:59,056 --> 00:05:01,190
content and learning path in real time.

73
00:05:03,290 --> 00:05:06,890
The AI learning assistant supports
both students and teachers.

74
00:05:07,490 --> 00:05:10,548
For students, it provides hints
and explanations rather than

75
00:05:10,599 --> 00:05:13,810
simply giving answers, so they
can solve problems on their own.

76
00:05:14,410 --> 00:05:17,582
For teachers, it shows each
student’s progress and challenges,

77
00:05:17,633 --> 00:05:20,600
so they can guide and coach
each student more effectively.

78
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:25,890
This screen shows a student’s
progress on the knowledge map.

79
00:05:26,490 --> 00:05:30,286
The bottom shows concepts already
studied, the middle shows concepts

80
00:05:30,342 --> 00:05:33,580
being learned, and the top
shows concepts not yet studied.

81
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:38,304
Each objective is classified
as mastered, needs

82
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:41,040
more practice, learning
gap, or not yet studied.

83
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:47,360
These statuses are updated whenever new
assessment and learning data come in.

84
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:50,842
So even if a concept was
studied earlier, any gap that

85
00:05:50,895 --> 00:05:53,990
appears is filled, and the next
learning path is adjusted.

86
00:05:54,590 --> 00:05:57,741
Students don’t repeat what they
already know, they get the practice

87
00:05:57,788 --> 00:06:00,610
they need, and each student
follows their own learning path.

88
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:04,650
We expect four key benefits.

89
00:06:05,350 --> 00:06:08,076
First, we can develop and
validate content aligned

90
00:06:08,131 --> 00:06:10,530
with each country’s
curriculum more quickly.

91
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:16,571
Second, we can personalize learning
objectives and the amount of practice

92
00:06:16,625 --> 00:06:20,890
across POD and online learning, delivering
the right content at the right time.

93
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:26,600
Third, we can fill learning gaps
and adjust each student’s learning

94
00:06:26,654 --> 00:06:29,940
path in real time, based on their
understanding and progress.

95
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:35,792
Finally, by considering academic
achievement alongside the

96
00:06:35,856 --> 00:06:39,932
JEI Self-Learning Index, or
JEI-SLI, we can show each student’s

97
00:06:39,996 --> 00:06:43,360
growth over time to students,
teachers, and parents.

98
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:48,020
Students are compared not with others,
but with their own past progress.

99
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:52,794
Turning 50 years of
learning design expertise

100
00:06:52,854 --> 00:06:55,290
into knowledge AI can understand and use.

101
00:06:55,890 --> 00:06:57,670
This is where the project begins.

102
00:06:58,370 --> 00:07:01,664
On this foundation, we’ll develop
learning content for each

103
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:05,350
market more quickly, and build
JEI’s own AI personalized learning

104
00:07:05,406 --> 00:07:08,700
platform that supports every
student’s learning and growth.

105
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:14,537
Through this, JEI will further advance the
value of individualized, ability-based

106
00:07:14,599 --> 00:07:18,890
learning, and set a new global
standard for AI-powered math learning.

